# 14. Required agent workflow

The agent must process one pressure through seven non-substitutable passes.

## Pass 1 — Fix the edge

The agent states only:

[
A\rightarrow B?
]

It may not begin broad research until the exact transition is fixed.

Example:

[
\text{causal integration}
\rightarrow
\text{phenomenal co-presence}?
]

---

## Pass 2 — Establish the antecedent

Determine whether (A) is:

* phenomenologically secure;
* experimentally supported;
* theoretically inferred;
* textually asserted;
* metaphysically assumed.

The agent may not attack or defend (A\rightarrow B) while silently treating (A) as established.

---

## Pass 3 — Retrieve direct arguments

A source qualifies only if it supplies at least one premise bearing directly upon the edge.

A paper about consciousness generally does not qualify for FPG-05 unless it addresses co-presence or subject boundary selection.

A Sanskrit passage mentioning *ātman* does not qualify unless it argues for unity, ownership, participation or continuity.

---

## Pass 4 — Reconstruct separately

For each source record:

[
\text{textual premises}
]

[
\text{scholarly reconstruction}
]

[
\text{agent reconstruction}
]

as separate fields.

The agent may not present its strongest reconstruction as though it were verbatim doctrine.

---

## Pass 5 — Generate countermodels

A countermodel must accept as much of the antecedent as possible while rejecting the consequent.

Example:

[
\text{causal integration}
]

without:

[
\text{phenomenal unity}.
]

This is stronger than merely denying the entire theory.

---

## Pass 6 — Identify the decisive missing premise

Every research run ends with one sentence of the form:

> The argument succeeds only if (P), but (P) is currently unsupported because (R).

No source collection is complete until this sentence exists.

---

## Pass 7 — Generate discriminating programmes

Each unresolved premise produces:

* an empirical programme;
* a textual programme;
* a formal programme;
* a cross-tradition adversarial programme.

The output is not another essay.

It is the next executable research branch.

